er products. The Retail segment operates convenience stores and fuel retail outlets that sell gasoline, diesel, and retail merchandise, such as soft drinks, prepared food, and other sundries under the Hele, 76, and nomnom brands, as well as unattended cardlock stations. The Logistics segment owns and operates terminals, pipelines, trucking operations, marine vessels, storage facilities, loading and truck racks, and rail facilities for the movement of ethanol, petroleum, and refined products; and a jet fuel storage facility and pipeline that serves Ellsworth Air Force Base in South Dakota. The company also holds interest in crude storage tanks and a crude oil pipeline that provides access to crude oil from power river basin; and refined products pipeline. In addition, it owns and operates a single point mooring, a marine terminal, a unit train-capable rail loading terminal, manifest rail siding, a truck rack, and a proprietary jet fuel pipeline that serves Joint Base Lewis McChord. The company was formerly known as Par Petroleum Corporation and changed its name to Par Pacific Holdings, Inc. in October 2015. Par Pacific Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1984 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William  Monteleone | President, CEO & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $4.2M ranks in the above the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 41%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $169K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Par Pacific Holdings, Inc. Comm is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.7B market cap on $7.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +55.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $296M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $16.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 62% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here's Why Par Petroleum (PARR) is a Strong Growth Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029489/here-s-why-par-petroleum-parr-is-a-strong-growth-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3029489","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577504.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why (PARR) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/Why_PARR_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_111226105001_1794541801.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794541801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Par Pacific Holdings (PARR) Stock Dropped, What Is Behind The Latest Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-parr/par-pacific-holdings/news/par-pacific-holdings-parr-stock-dropped-what-is-behind-the-l","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794421839.761,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.942,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Should Strong Earnings Report Require Action From Par Pacific Holdings (PARR) Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplyw